# Finder

A finder searches one defined collection and uses relevant filters to narrow its results. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/finder/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## One composition with contextual variants

Use the [search-filter pattern](../patterns/search-filter.html) for query, facet, count and reset behaviour, and the [search-input component](../../components/search-input.html) for the field itself. This page owns the collection composition. The eleven retained source routes below explain applicability; they are not eleven new household services.

| Retained source context | Household boundary |
| --- | --- |
| [Case studies](finder/case-studies-finder.html) | Curated project evidence; label synthetic examples and tested records accurately. |
| [Organisations](finder/departments-agencies-public-bodies-finder.html) | Integration or provider context only; no invented government affiliation. |
| [Groups](finder/groups-finder.html) | Explicitly configured groups; matching names do not prove membership. |
| [Contacts](finder/hmrc-contacts-finder.html) | Verified support destinations; no invented contact details or response times. |
| [People](finder/people-finder.html) | Private roles only; native account permissions and presence privacy remain separate. |
| [Search](finder/search.html) | A stated documentation scope; do not blend it with private household data. |
| [Specialist documents](finder/specialist-document-finder.html) | Model and revision context; a name match does not establish compatibility. |
| [Data sets](finder/statistical-data-sets-finder.html) | Real measurements or existing exports; no imaginary download endpoint. |
| [Broad purposes](finder/supergroup-finder.html) | Predictable guidance categories; no replacement for native area or domain taxonomy. |
| [Projects and events](finder/topical-events-finder.html) | Current and archived projects distinguished by actual status and dates. |
| [Worldwide organisations](finder/world-organisation-finder.html) | No direct household equivalent; multi-home discovery is not implemented. |

Every variant keeps its existing examples and source attribution. Extend a collection only when its records, permissions and destinations actually exist; do not infer live discovery or account management from a directory layout.

## When to use it

The household equivalent is a device, automation, guide or maintenance-record finder with a clearly stated scope. Start from the permitted native dataset. Explain whether the search covers entity names, friendly names, model numbers or document text. Do not combine unrelated datasets without labelling the result types.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a labelled search, useful facets, a result count and clear result links. Each result needs a stable title and enough metadata to tell it apart. Keep the current criteria when returning from a result. Provide explicit loading, no-match and unavailable states. The local finder filters three fixed example records, with readable disclosures, a matching count and a clear-filters action. It does not search Home Assistant. Without JavaScript, all records remain available and the form cannot submit.

## Home Assistant boundary

This is a reference pattern; the theme does not replace HA search or invent a registry endpoint. The child pages document every official finder variant and its local applicability. Government directory types that do not fit a household are recorded as boundaries, not implemented as fake services.

